            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I expect generated *.so objects to not have this `libpython` linkage.\n\nI agree that it shouldn't be there. Linkage against libpython is for CPython, not for its extension modules.\n\nThe Python headers shouldn't pull in anything that adds library dependencies, so it's entirely up to the extension module to define its own direct dependencies, and only those. Everything else should be resolved at import time when loading the extension module into Python.\n\nSearching for `current_py_cc_libs` suggests that it's really only meant for embedding and should be removed from the extension module build.\nhttps://github.com/bazel-contrib/rules_python/blob/9f3ab0630537ce54356d78a28f4618d926ec31ce/docs/howto/linking-libpython.md\n\n> Can I post a PR for the fix?\n\nPlease do.\n\n> What level of testing would I need to show there is no regression?\n\nWe don't use bazel at all, so there is no testing. It's a build support script that we ship for the convenience of users. That's what makes decisions on it difficult.",
